# Pass 26 — Production Readiness. `/dist` and `/build` here only ever matched a
# `dist`/`build` folder at the repo ROOT — this project's own build script
# (`npm run build` -> `tsc && copyfiles ...` in api/package.json) produces `api/dist`,
# a nested path these root-anchored patterns never covered. 68 stale generated .js
# files were found checked into git as a direct result while auditing this — removed
# from tracking in the same commit as this fix. Changed to unanchored `dist/` so it
# matches at any depth.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.DS_Store

# `.env` alone only protects a FUTURE `.env` (at any depth, unanchored patterns match
# recursively) from ever being added — it does not cover `.env.production`,
# `.env.test`, etc. Extended to `.env.*` with an explicit carve-out for the one
# environment file that's supposed to be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Pass 22's winston logger and Pass 25's Jest coverage reports are both real,
# generated-on-disk artifacts with no reason to ever be version controlled.
logs/
*.log
coverage/
